{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Like a House on Fire"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Test of Friendship "}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le18ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Causative - Get/Have - Solving Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the causative verbs get/have when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">My boss <span class=\"strong\">had me do</span> an emergency project."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this sentence the boss asks or persuades you to do an emergency project."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the causative is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "have + object + verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Milton <span class=\"strong\">had his son come down</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "or "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + get + object + Infinitive "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got Cindy to join</span> us as well."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to <span class=\"underline\">convince someone to do something</span>.<br> <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral and implies that you give someone the responsibility to do something."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have to get someone to play with us."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I better get the bartender to check the keg."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Milton had his son come down. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I got Cindy to join us as well."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Need + Passive Infinitive and Need +Verb+ing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use <span class=\"italic\">need + passive infinitive</span> and <span class=\"italic\">need +verb+ing</span> to talk about things that need to be done. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use these structures to focus on the <span class=\"strong\">thing</span> that needs doing, not the person who is doing it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + Need + Passive Infinitive"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The dishes <span class=\"strong\">need to be washed</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The subject of the sentence is the thing that needs doing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + Need + Verb + ing"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The floor <span class=\"strong\">needs sweeping</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">need</span> with a gerund (v-ing), it has a passive meaning. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The dishes need to be washed."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The tables need bussing."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The floor needs sweeping and my tables need to be served."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cover for"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to replace someone in a duty "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll get Tanya to cover for you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about self-improvement."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hustle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move or act energetically and rapidly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now hustle down here."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lose your mind "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become mentally ill  or to start behaving in a silly or strange way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think I'm going to lose my mind."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "worth it"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sufficiently good, important, or interesting to be treated or regarded "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For me, it was worth it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dejectedly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in an unhappy and disappointed way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The coach spoke dejectedly after his team lost the game."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "animated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "full of life and energy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He speaks in such an animated way."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on me"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "this means that the person speaking will pay the whole amount of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Take a cab. It's on me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner describe the characteristics of a perfect friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Individually, write 200 words on things you could do to become a better friend. Include examples of behavior you would like to change."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about things that need to be done in your analysis."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about solving problems in your writing."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I self reflect on personal behaviour"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express things I have to get/have to become a better friend. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze things that I need to do in my analysis."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can react to things going wrong and respond to difficult questions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about things that need to be done."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about solving problems."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What things would you like to change about yourself? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How would you go about making these changes?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_a